      "message": "Re OpTypeMatrix. Based on the spec: https://www.khronos.org/registry/SPIR-V/specs/unified1/SPIRV.html#:~:text\u003dOpCompositeConstruct\n\n\"... top-level members/elements/components/columns have the same type as the types of the operands, with one exception. The exception is that for constructing a vector, the operands may also be vectors with the same component type as the Result Type component type.\"\n\nRe structs, OpCompositeExtract is allowed, and we use it in our implementation of `writeStructComparison` (but not in `FieldAccess` since that wants an lvalue/pointer). I think this is working as expected (one struct field \u003d one component).",
